# 3xui-dashboard — SECRETS.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Non-secret config goes in
# config.yaml (see config.yaml.example). Settings editable in the admin
# panel (registration, email rules, branding, OIDC, traffic thresholds, …)
# live in the database, NOT here. Real environment variables override both
# files.
#
# Source of truth for keys: internal/config/config.go.

# =============================================================================
# REQUIRED — bootstrap secrets. These can't live in the DB (they're needed
# before the DB is reachable / before you can log in).
# =============================================================================

# Postgres connection string (contains the DB password).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASS@127.0.0.1:5432/dashboard?sslmode=disable

# JWT signing secret — at least 32 chars. Rotating it invalidates all
# in-flight sessions. Don't share between deployments.
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-32-plus-char-random-string

# Admin login. If ADMIN_PASSWORD is blank, a random one is generated and
# printed to stderr on first boot — save it back here for restarts.
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# =============================================================================
# KEY-ENCRYPTION KEY — encrypts WireGuard peer keys at rest.
# =============================================================================
# Leave blank to disable WireGuard features. When set, MUST stay out of the
# DB (it protects DB data) and is NOT safely rotatable: rotating it makes
# every existing wg_peers row undecryptable — re-provision every WG peer.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
WG_MASTER_KEY=

# Encrypts secret SETTINGS at rest in the DB (SMTP/notify/payment creds, as
# those integrations move to panel-managed). Same KEK rules: keep it out of
# the DB; rotating it makes existing encrypted settings undecryptable. Blank
# = secret settings can't be stored in the DB (they stay in this file).
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# INTEGRATION SECRETS — these integrations are slated to move into the admin
# panel (DB) later; for now their secrets live here and their non-secret
# config in config.yaml. All optional.
# =============================================================================

# SMTP password (host/port/from/username are in config.yaml).
SMTP_PASSWORD=

# Alipay — PEM-encoded keys. AppID + gateway/URLs are in config.yaml.
# ALIPAY_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----"
# ALIPAY_PUBLIC_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\n...\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----"

# Stripe — test/live distinguished by the key prefix. Currency/URLs in config.yaml.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# Notify channel credentials. Routing (notify_routes) is in config.yaml.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=
# FEISHU_WEBHOOK_URL=

# =============================================================================
# OPTIONAL — seed remote 3x-ui nodes on first boot (carries API tokens, hence
# a secret). Matched by name; existing nodes updated. JSON array of
# {name, access_url | host/port, api_token, area, province, enabled}.
# Most operators add nodes from the admin UI instead — see docs/operator/.
# =============================================================================
# BOOTSTRAP_NODES_JSON='[{"name":"US Node","access_url":"https://node.example.com:2053/panel","api_token":"replace-me","enabled":true}]'
